<title>USA: World Bank approves $120 mln loan for Jordan.</title>
<headline>World Bank approves $120 mln loan for Jordan.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The World Bank said on Thursday it had approved a $120 million loan to help Jordan with economic reforms.</p>
<p>The loan will back reforms aimed at increasing competition and exports, modernising the financial system, introducing best practice business laws and privatisating state companies.</p>
<p>The loan is for 17 years, including a four-year grace period, at the bank's standard variable rate, the bank said in a statement.</p>
</text>
